From: xiaobao <xiaobao@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: rockchip: probe asynchronously

On ROCEOS K50S MAX (RK3568, PCIe3.0 x2 bifurcated 1+1 with two RTL8125),
the lane1 endpoint (behind pcie3x1/fe270000) only becomes trainable
AFTER the pcie3x2 (lane0, bifurcation master) controller probes, because
its PERST# is wired to the x2 controller's reset line. With synchronous
probing this can never work: pcie3x2 only starts probing after pcie3x1's
probe returns, i.e. after pcie3x1's dw_pcie_wait_for_link() window has
already expired ("Phy link never came up"), and making that window
longer merely postpones pcie3x2's probe as well. Base-dtsi node reorder
is fragile against the istoreos-24.10 patch series pre-image, and dtc
/delete-node/ + re-declare does not change FDT node order.

Mark the driver PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS so all Rockchip PCIe host
controllers probe in parallel: pcie3x2 then pulses the shared PERST#
immediately, the lane1 endpoint comes alive, and pcie3x1's (extended)
link-wait window catches the training. Controllers are independent
(reset/clk/regulator frameworks are thread-safe; the shared pcie30phy
is serialized by phy-core's mutex + refcounting). PCI domains and bus
numbering come from DT and are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: xiaobao <xiaobao@local>
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
index 05ff855..2409f5f 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
@@ -381,6 +381,7 @@ static struct platform_driver rockchip_pcie_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name	= "rockchip-dw-pcie",
 		.of_match_table = rockchip_pcie_of_match,
+		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
 	},
 	.probe = rockchip_pcie_probe,
